@SYSTEM_TITLE
; `INITRAND` restores whatever `RANDDATA` currently holds - it does NOT
; auto-snapshot the live generator first. A fresh game's `RANDDATA` is a
; plain `int[625]` array (all zero, like any other undeclared savedata),
; so `INITRAND` with no preceding `DUMPRAND` loads that all-zero state,
; which real Emuera's own SFMT-19937 generator treats as a degenerate
; fixed point (draws come back `0` forever) - verified by actually running
; Emuera1818_kr3.exe with this exact draw/INITRAND sequence and no prior
; DUMPRAND. So this test must call `DUMPRAND` first to snapshot the state
; being tested, exactly like a real script's save/restore round trip would.
DUMPRAND
LOCAL = RAND:1000
INITRAND
CALL ASSERT(LOCAL == RAND:1000)

RANDOMIZE 2
LOCAL = RAND:1000
RANDOMIZE 2
CALL ASSERT(LOCAL == RAND:1000)

@ASSERT(ARG)
SIF !ARG
    THROW ERROR

